## polymarket-quant-desk configuration
##
## This configuration file defines the file paths and credentials for your installation.
## Documentation below shows you how to configure this and sign up for the necessary onlines
## services to get the data you need and execute trades.
##
## In addition to the standard configuration, you may add your own variables to this file as you
## develop your own datasets, explorations and trading bots. If new variables are introduced
## upstream in the GitHub project, you will be responsible to merge them into your local .env file.
##
## Estimated setup time: 30+ minutes
## 

## File storage
##
## Use a location with 1+ TB free space and SSD or faster (i.e. ≥ 400 MB/s sequential read, ≥ 10,000
## random 4K read IOPS).
##
## Every dataset directory holds immutable, finalized data and gets its own variable, so you can
## put each one wherever you like, including object storage on a cloud VPS deployment.
##
## HOT_DIR and SCRATCH_DIR are shared by every program in the project and must be on local block
## storage. Each program names its own files inside them, after the dataset it serves.
##
## - HOT_DIR holds mutable DuckDB databases of in-progress work. Losing it costs you a rescrape.
## - SCRATCH_DIR is where DuckDB spills during large queries. A single query can spill 50+ GB, so
##   do not point this at /tmp, which is memory backed on many systems. Nothing here is durable.
##
DATA_BASE_DIR=/Volumes/polymarket-quant-desk
HOT_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/raw_data/hot
SCRATCH_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/scratch
POLYGON_CONTRACT_EVENTS_V3_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/raw_data/cold/polygon_contract_events_v3
TOKEN_ID_MAP_V1_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/derived_data/token_id_map_v1
FILLS_V1_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/derived_data/fills_v1
CONDITION_BY_BLOCK_V1_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/derived_data/condition_by_block_v1
CONDITION_BY_10K_V1_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/derived_data/condition_by_10k_v1
ACCOUNT_CONDITION_BY_10K_V1_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/derived_data/account_condition_by_10k_v1
ACCOUNT_BY_10K_V1_DIR=${DATA_BASE_DIR}/derived_data/account_by_10k_v1

## Online services
##
## You will need access to several services to get necessary data and execute trades on your quant
## desk. Following are services confirmed to work with polymarket-quant-desk. Each offers a free
## tier unless otherwise noted. Other competing services may also work.
##
## POLYGON_RPC_URL (HTTPS JSON-RPC: scrape, balances, on-chain txs)
## POLYGON_WS_URL (WebSocket JSON-RPC: --listen rpc for live fills)
## - dRPC (https://drpc.org/)
## - Infura (https://infura.io/)
## - Chainstack (https://chainstack.com/)
##   Chainstack dedicated: HTTPS nd-….p2pify.com and WSS ws-nd-….p2pify.com.
##   If POLYGON_WS_URL is unset, that pair is derived from POLYGON_RPC_URL.
##
## ETHERSCAN_API_KEY (for contract source code)
## - Etherscan (https://etherscan.io/)
##
## (OPTIONAL) POLYNODE_API_KEY (to execute trades)
## - Polynode (https://polynode.dev/)
##
POLYGON_RPC_URL=
POLYGON_WS_URL=
ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=
POLYNODE_API_KEY=

## BUILDER_CODE (public bytes32, not a secret)
## Copy from https://polymarket.com/settings?tab=builder
## Stamped into every v2 order. The landed OrderFilled.builder field equals this value.
## BUILDER_API_KEY, BUILDER_SECRET, and BUILDER_PASSPHRASE stay on the relayer
## (redeem, merge, wrap). They do not set the order field.
BUILDER_CODE=
